IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 2, GENERAL EMPOWERING PROVISIONS AND THE EXERCISE OF POWERS (ss 40 to 53).
-- Each section here gives a power, or removes a doubt about one. A power is a relation between the holder and whoever is subject to it
-- (see "Jural relations" in NOTES.md). The facts are inputs; where the section is silent the answer is NOTHING, not a guess.
-- Each rule is a provision of Part 2, so section 9(1) (nz-part2-principles.l4) says first whether it applies to the legislation in question.

§ `Section 40 -- Authority to make secondary legislation`

-- src:295 | It is not necessary for secondary legislation to refer to facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the legislation can be made.
-- (1) It is not necessary for secondary legislation to refer to facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the legislation can be made.
-- src:294 | 40 Authority to make secondary legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 40(1) (src:294) (src:295)
GIVEN `the secondary legislation refers to the facts, circumstances or preconditions that must exist before it can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is necessary for the secondary legislation to refer to the preconditions for making it` `the secondary legislation refers to the facts, circumstances or preconditions that must exist before it can be made` MEANS FALSE

-- (2) Secondary legislation is not invalid just because the legislation under which it is expressed to have been made does not authorise its making as long as its making is
-- authorised by other legislation. If neither authorises its making, the section is silent.
-- src:296 | Secondary legislation is not invalid just because the legislation under which it is expressed to have been made does not authorise its making as long as its making is authorised by other legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 40(2) (src:296)
GIVEN `the legislation it is expressed to be made under authorises its making` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other legislation authorises its making` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`secondary legislation is invalid because the legislation it is expressed to be made under does not authorise it` `the legislation it is expressed to be made under authorises its making` `other legislation authorises its making` MEANS
    IF `the legislation it is expressed to be made under authorises its making` OR `other legislation authorises its making`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 41 -- Secondary legislation may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation`

-- src:298 | A power to make secondary legislation (the main secondary legislation) under one Act (the main Act) includes a power to make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation made by the same person (whether or not made under the same Act).
-- src:299 | An amendment is consequential for the purposes of this section if it is consequential on the passing or making of either or both of the following:
-- src:300 | the main Act or any amendment to it:
-- src:301 | the main secondary legislation or any amendment to it.
-- (1) A power to make secondary legislation (the main secondary legislation) under one Act (the main Act) includes a power to make consequential amendments to other secondary
-- legislation made by the same person (whether or not made under the same Act). (2) An amendment is consequential if it is consequential on the passing or making of either or both of
-- the main Act or any amendment to it, or the main secondary legislation or any amendment to it.
-- src:297 | 41 Secondary legislation may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 41(1) and (2) (src:297) (src:298-301)
GIVEN `the other secondary legislation was made by the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is consequential on the main Act or an amendment to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is consequential on the main secondary legislation or an amendment to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` `the other secondary legislation was made by the same person` `the amendment is consequential on the main Act or an amendment to it` `the amendment is consequential on the main secondary legislation or an amendment to it` MEANS
        `the other secondary legislation was made by the same person`
    AND (`the amendment is consequential on the main Act or an amendment to it` OR `the amendment is consequential on the main secondary legislation or an amendment to it`)

-- (3) The only facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the consequential amendments are made are those (if any) for making the main secondary legislation.
-- src:302 | The only facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the consequential amendments are made are those (if any) for making the main secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 41(3) (src:302)
GIVEN `the preconditions for making the main secondary legislation` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the preconditions for making consequential amendments` `the preconditions for making the main secondary legislation` MEANS
    `the preconditions for making the main secondary legislation`

§ `Section 42 -- Amendments made to secondary legislation by Act do not prevent later amendments`

-- src:303 | 42 Amendments made to secondary legislation by Act do not prevent later amendments
-- src:304 | Secondary legislation amended or replaced by an Act may be amended, revoked, or replaced by later secondary legislation as if the amendment or replacement had been made by secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 42 (src:303) (src:304)
GIVEN `the secondary legislation was amended or replaced by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`later secondary legislation may amend, revoke or replace secondary legislation amended or replaced by an Act` `the secondary legislation was amended or replaced by an Act` MEANS
    `the secondary legislation was amended or replaced by an Act`

§ `Section 43 -- When powers can be exercised before commencement`

DECLARE `Kind of act done before commencement` IS ONE OF
    `making secondary legislation or another instrument`
    `making secondary legislation`
    `making another instrument`
    `serving a notice or document`
    `serving a notice`
    `serving a document`
    `appointing a person to an office`
    `establishing a body of persons`
    `conferring or imposing a legal position on a person`
    `conferring a legal position on a person`
    `imposing a legal position on a person`
    `doing another act or thing for the purposes of the legislation`
    `doing an act or thing that is not for the purposes of the legislation`

-- src:307 | A power conferred by legislation may be exercised before the legislation comes into force or takes effect to—
-- src:308 | make secondary legislation or another instrument; or
-- src:309 | serve a notice or document; or
-- src:310 | appoint a person to an office; or
-- src:311 | establish a body of persons; or
-- src:312 | confer or impose on a person a right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity (a legal position); or
-- src:313 | do any other act or thing for the purposes of the legislation.
-- src:314 | However, the power may be exercised only if the exercise of the power is necessary or desirable—
-- src:315 | to bring the legislation into operation; or
-- src:316 | in connection with bringing the legislation into operation.
-- (1) A power conferred by legislation may be exercised before the legislation comes into force or takes effect to (a) make secondary legislation or another instrument; (b) serve a notice or document;
-- (c) appoint a person to an office; (d) establish a body of persons; (e) confer or impose a legal position; (f) do any other act or thing for the purposes of the legislation.
-- (2) However, the power may be exercised only if the exercise is necessary or desirable to bring the legislation into operation, or in connection with bringing it into operation.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): s 43(1) is a closed list of grants and (2) is an "only if", so an act that is not for the purposes of the legislation, or an exercise that is not necessary or desirable, is not given by the section: JUST FALSE.
-- src:306 | 43 When powers can be exercised before commencement
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 43(1) and (2) (src:306) (src:307-316)
GIVEN act IS A `Kind of act done before commencement`
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` act `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` necessary MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `doing an act or thing that is not for the purposes of the legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST necessary

-- (3) Subsection (1) applies as if the legislation that confers the power, and all other legislation relevant to the power's exercise and not yet commenced, had commenced; and as if a legal position
-- that would be conferred or imposed by such legislation has been conferred or imposed.
-- src:318 | the legislation that confers the power, and all other legislation that is relevant to the power’s exercise and that has not yet commenced, had commenced; and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 43(3)(a) (src:318)
GIVEN `the legislation confers the power or is relevant to the power's exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation has not yet commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the legislation is treated as having commenced for the purposes of section 43(1)` `the legislation confers the power or is relevant to the power's exercise` `the legislation has not yet commenced` MEANS
    `the legislation confers the power or is relevant to the power's exercise` AND `the legislation has not yet commenced`

-- src:319 | a legal position that would be conferred or imposed by legislation that is relevant to the power’s exercise, and that has not yet commenced, has been conferred or imposed.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 43(3)(b) (src:319)
GIVEN `the legal position would be conferred or imposed by legislation relevant to the power's exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that legislation has not yet commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the legal position is treated as having been conferred or imposed for the purposes of section 43(1)` `the legal position would be conferred or imposed by legislation relevant to the power's exercise` `that legislation has not yet commenced` MEANS
    `the legal position would be conferred or imposed by legislation relevant to the power's exercise` AND `that legislation has not yet commenced`

§ `Section 44 -- Limit on when pre-commencement exercise of powers takes effect`

-- src:320 | 44 Limit on when pre-commencement exercise of powers takes effect
-- src:321 | Anything that results from the exercise of a power under section 43 may take effect only on and after the commencement of the legislation that confers the power.
-- src:322 | However, that limit does not apply if the exercise of the power is necessary or desirable—
-- src:323 | to bring the legislation into operation; or
-- src:324 | in connection with bringing the legislation into operation; or
-- src:325 | to amend, revoke, or replace anything previously done in reliance on section 43.
-- (1) Anything that results from the exercise of a power under section 43 may take effect only on and after the commencement of the legislation that confers the power.
-- (2) However, that limit does not apply if the exercise is necessary or desirable (a) to bring the legislation into operation; (b) in connection with bringing it into operation; or
-- (c) to amend, revoke, or replace anything previously done in reliance on section 43. Day level: the commencement takes effect at the start of its day (s 27).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 44 (src:320) (src:321-325)
GIVEN `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day the legislation that confers the power commences` IS A DATE
      `the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation, or in connection with that` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is necessary or desirable to amend, revoke or replace something previously done in reliance on section 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` `the day it takes effect` `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` `the day the legislation that confers the power commences` `if` `the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation, or in connection with that` `or` `the exercise is necessary or desirable to amend, revoke or replace something previously done in reliance on section 43` MEANS
        (`the day it takes effect` AT LEAST `the day the legislation that confers the power commences`)
     OR `the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation, or in connection with that`
     OR `the exercise is necessary or desirable to amend, revoke or replace something previously done in reliance on section 43`

§ `Section 45 -- Power to appoint person to an office includes related powers`

-- The printed items are members, and so is each thing an item names (ruling C): remove, suspend, reappoint, reinstate; absent temporarily, absent permanently; incapacitated temporarily, permanently; removed, suspended.
-- Paragraph (c)(iv) covers only an incapacity "in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty"; one that does not is a member of its own, and the Act is silent on it.
DECLARE `Related power of an appointer` IS ONE OF
    `remove or suspend a person from the office`
    `remove a person from the office`
    `suspend a person from the office`
    `reappoint or reinstate a person to the office`
    `reappoint a person to the office`
    `reinstate a person to the office`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who has vacated the office voluntarily`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who has died`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent temporarily or permanently`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent temporarily`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent permanently`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated temporarily in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated permanently in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated in a way that does not affect the performance of that person's duty`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who has been removed or suspended from the office`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who has been removed from the office`
    `appoint another person in place of a person who has been suspended from the office`
    `another power`

-- src:326 | 45 Power to appoint person to an office includes related powers
-- src:327 | The power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to—
-- src:328 | remove or suspend a person from the office:
-- src:329 | reappoint or reinstate a person to the office:
-- src:330 | appoint (temporarily or permanently, and for all or limited purposes) another person in place of a person who—
-- src:331 | has vacated the office voluntarily (for example, by resigning); or
-- src:332 | has died; or
-- src:333 | is absent temporarily or permanently; or
-- src:334 | is incapacitated temporarily or permanently in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty; or
-- src:335 | has been removed or suspended from the office.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 45 (src:326) (src:327-335)
GIVEN power IS A `Related power of an appointer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` power MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `another power` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated in a way that does not affect the performance of that person's duty` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 46 -- Power to do things may be exercised to correct errors`

-- src:336 | 46 Power to do things may be exercised to correct errors
-- src:337 | The power to do anything may be exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power.
-- src:338 | Subsection (1) applies even though the power is not generally capable of being exercised more than once.
-- (1) The power to do anything may be exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power. (2) Subsection (1) applies even though the power is not generally capable of being exercised more than once.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 46 (src:336) (src:337-338)
GIVEN `it is exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised again` `it is exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power` `even if the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` `the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` MEANS
    IF `it is exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 47 -- Powers of office holder may be exercised by acting office holders`

DECLARE `Who exercises an office holder's power` IS ONE OF
    `the holder's deputy lawfully acting in the office`
    `a person for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office`
    `a person for the time being lawfully holding the office`
    `a person for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the office`
    `someone else`

-- src:339 | 47 Powers of office holder may be exercised by acting office holders
-- src:340 | A power conferred on the holder of an office, other than a Minister of the Crown, may be exercised by 1 or both of the following:
-- src:341 | a person who is the holder’s deputy lawfully acting in the office:
-- src:342 | a person who is for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office.
-- A power conferred on the holder of an office, other than a Minister of the Crown, may be exercised by 1 or both of the following: the holder's deputy lawfully acting in the office; a person for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): "other than a Minister of the Crown" only draws the edge of the section, it does not forbid, so for a Minister the answer stays NOTHING; for any other office holder the section gives the two persons named, and someone else is off its closed list (JUST FALSE).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 47 (src:339) (src:340-342)
GIVEN person IS A `Who exercises an office holder's power`
      `the office holder is a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` person `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` `the office holder is a Minister of the Crown` MEANS
    IF `the office holder is a Minister of the Crown`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `the holder's deputy lawfully acting in the office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person for the time being lawfully holding the office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `someone else` THEN JUST FALSE

§ `Section 48 -- Power to make includes power to amend or revoke`

DECLARE `What is done to legislation or an instrument that was made` IS ONE OF
    `amending it`
    `revoking it`
    `replacing it`
    `something else`

-- src:344 | The power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument includes the power to—
-- src:345 | amend or revoke the legislation or instrument:
-- src:346 | replace the legislation or instrument.
-- (1) The power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument includes the power to amend or revoke the legislation or instrument, and to replace it.
-- (2) Requirements that apply in relation to making the secondary legislation or other instrument also apply, with all necessary modifications, in relation to its amendment, revocation, or replacement.
-- src:343 | 48 Power to make includes power to amend or revoke
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 48(1) (src:343) (src:344-346)
GIVEN action IS A `What is done to legislation or an instrument that was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to make secondary legislation or an instrument includes the power to` action MEANS
    CONSIDER action
    WHEN `amending it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `revoking it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `replacing it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:347 | Requirements that apply in relation to making the secondary legislation or other instrument also apply, with all necessary modifications, in relation to its amendment, revocation, or replacement.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 48(2) (src:347)
GIVEN action IS A `What is done to legislation or an instrument that was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the requirements for making it also apply, with necessary modifications, to` action MEANS
    CONSIDER action
    WHEN `amending it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `revoking it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `replacing it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 49 -- Power to make different provision for classes of matters`

DECLARE `Way of using a power to make secondary legislation or an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `making it with respect to some only of the matters`
    `making it with respect to a particular class or classes of the matters`
    `making different provision with respect to different matters`
    `making different provision with respect to different classes of matters`
    `another way`

-- src:348 | 49 Power to make different provision for classes of matters
-- src:349 | This section applies to legislation that confers on a person a power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument with respect to particular matters (however the matters are described).
-- src:350 | The power includes a power—
-- src:351 | to make the secondary legislation or instrument with respect to some only of those matters or with respect to a particular class or particular classes of those matters; and
-- src:352 | to make different provision with respect to different matters or different classes of matters.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 49 (src:348) (src:349-352)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of using a power to make secondary legislation or an instrument`
      `the legislation confers a power to make secondary legislation or an instrument with respect to particular matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power includes the power to use it by` way `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` `the legislation confers a power to make secondary legislation or an instrument with respect to particular matters` MEANS
    IF `the legislation confers a power to make secondary legislation or an instrument with respect to particular matters`
    THEN CONSIDER way
         WHEN `another way` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 50 -- Power to identify matters using classes`

-- src:353 | 50 Power to identify matters using classes
-- src:354 | This section applies to legislation that confers on a person a power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument—
-- src:355 | declaring, prescribing, or specifying a matter; or
-- src:356 | doing anything in relation to a matter.
-- src:357 | In exercising the power, the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters.
-- The section applies to a power to make secondary legislation or another instrument declaring, prescribing or specifying a matter, or doing anything in relation to a matter; the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 50 (src:353) (src:354-357)
GIVEN `the power is one of declaring, prescribing or specifying a matter, or doing anything in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters` `the power is one of declaring, prescribing or specifying a matter, or doing anything in relation to a matter` MEANS
    IF `the power is one of declaring, prescribing or specifying a matter, or doing anything in relation to a matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 51 -- Exercise or performance of powers, functions, and duties more than once`

DECLARE `Power, duty or function` IS ONE OF
    `a power conferred by legislation`
    `a duty or function imposed by legislation`
    `a duty imposed by legislation`
    `a function imposed by legislation`

-- src:358 | 51 Exercise or performance of powers, functions, and duties more than once
-- src:359 | A power conferred by legislation may be exercised from time to time.
-- src:360 | A duty or function imposed by legislation may be performed from time to time.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 51 (src:358) (src:359-360)
GIVEN kind IS A `Power, duty or function`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it may be exercised or performed from time to time` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a power conferred by legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duty or function imposed by legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duty imposed by legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a function imposed by legislation` THEN TRUE

§ `Section 52 -- Use of approved or prescribed forms`

-- src:362 | 52 Use of approved or prescribed forms
-- src:363 | A form is not invalid just because it contains minor differences from an approved or a prescribed form as long as the form still has the same effect and is not misleading.
-- A form is not invalid just because it contains minor differences from an approved or a prescribed form as long as the form still has the same effect and is not misleading.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 52 (src:362) (src:363)
GIVEN `it contains only minor differences from the approved or prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it still has the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a form is invalid just because of its differences from the approved or prescribed form` `it contains only minor differences from the approved or prescribed form` `it still has the same effect` `it is misleading` MEANS
    IF `it contains only minor differences from the approved or prescribed form` AND `it still has the same effect` AND (NOT `it is misleading`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 53 -- Extension of power to approve or prescribe forms`

DECLARE `Part of power B` IS ONE OF
    `identify the information to be supplied or made available`
    `identify the information to be supplied`
    `identify the information to be made available`
    `approve or prescribe a method, format or medium for supplying or making information available`
    `approve or prescribe a method for supplying or making information available`
    `approve or prescribe a format for supplying or making information available`
    `approve or prescribe a medium for supplying or making information available`
    `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form or a method, format or medium`
    `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form`
    `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a method`
    `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a format`
    `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a medium`
    `another part`

-- src:365 | This section applies to a power (power A) conferred by legislation to approve or prescribe a form used to supply information that must or may be supplied to any person, or made available, for any purpose.
-- src:366 | Power A includes a power (power B) to do any 1 or more of the following:
-- src:367 | identify the information to be supplied or made available:
-- src:368 | approve or prescribe a method, format, or medium for supplying information or making information available:
-- src:369 | if power A is a power to prescribe a form, authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form or a method, format, or medium for supplying information or making information available.
-- Power A is a power conferred by legislation to approve or prescribe a form used to supply information. (2) Power A includes a power (power B) to do any 1 or more of: (a) identify the information to be supplied
-- or made available; (b) approve or prescribe a method, format, or medium; (c) if power A is a power to prescribe a form, authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form or a method, format, or medium.
-- src:364 | 53 Extension of power to approve or prescribe forms
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 53(1) and (2) (src:364) (src:365-369)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of power B`
      `power A is a power to prescribe a form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`power A includes the power to` part `when power A is a power to prescribe a form:` `power A is a power to prescribe a form` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `identify the information to be supplied or made available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `identify the information to be supplied` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `identify the information to be made available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `approve or prescribe a method, format or medium for supplying or making information available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `approve or prescribe a method for supplying or making information available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `approve or prescribe a format for supplying or making information available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `approve or prescribe a medium for supplying or making information available` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form or a method, format or medium` THEN
        IF `power A is a power to prescribe a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a form` THEN
        IF `power A is a power to prescribe a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a method` THEN
        IF `power A is a power to prescribe a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a format` THEN
        IF `power A is a power to prescribe a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `authorise a prescribed person to approve or prescribe a medium` THEN
        IF `power A is a power to prescribe a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `another part` THEN NOTHING

-- (3) Power B may be exercised in place of, or as well as, power A. (4) Information supplied or made available under power B complies with legislation that refers to, requires, or otherwise
-- operates with the form as if the information had been supplied or made available in an approved or a prescribed form.
-- src:370 | Power B may be exercised in place of, or as well as, power A.
-- src:371 | Information supplied or made available under power B complies with legislation that refers to, requires, or otherwise operates with the form as if the information had been supplied or made available in an approved or a prescribed form (and the legislation applies, with all necessary modifications, accordingly).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 53(3) and (4) (src:370-371)
GIVEN `the information was supplied or made available in the way power B provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the information complies with legislation that operates with the form` `the information was supplied or made available in the way power B provides` MEANS
    `the information was supplied or made available in the way power B provides`

-- (5) applies if power A is itself a power to make secondary legislation; and secondary legislation made under power A (and in reliance on power B in (2)(c)) authorises a person to approve or prescribe a form
-- and, in doing so, to determine the information to be supplied or made available; and the form, rather than the secondary legislation, will identify the information. (6) If it applies, the instrument by which
-- the person approves or prescribes the form is secondary legislation, and the secondary legislation referred to in (5)(b) must contain a statement to that effect.
-- src:372 | Subsection (6) applies if—
-- src:373 | power A is itself a power to make secondary legislation; and
-- src:374 | secondary legislation made under power A (and in reliance on the power B referred to in subsection (2)﻿(c)) authorises a person to approve or prescribe a form and, in doing so, to determine the information to be supplied or made available; and
-- src:375 | the form, rather than the secondary legislation, will identify the information to be supplied or made available.
-- src:376 | If this subsection applies,—
-- src:377 | the instrument by which the person approves or prescribes the form is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements); and
-- src:378 | the secondary legislation referred to in subsection (5)﻿(b) must contain a statement to that effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 53(5) and (6) (src:372-378)
GIVEN `power A is itself a power to make secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `secondary legislation made under power A and in reliance on power B authorises a person to approve or prescribe a form and to determine the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form, rather than the secondary legislation, identifies the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument approving or prescribing the form is secondary legislation, and the authorising secondary legislation must say so` `power A is itself a power to make secondary legislation` `secondary legislation made under power A and in reliance on power B authorises a person to approve or prescribe a form and to determine the information` `the form, rather than the secondary legislation, identifies the information` MEANS
        `power A is itself a power to make secondary legislation`
    AND `secondary legislation made under power A and in reliance on power B authorises a person to approve or prescribe a form and to determine the information`
    AND `the form, rather than the secondary legislation, identifies the information`
